# Drafted by Gemini (R15 side_print), edited.

~ cora_start
cora_beaudry [sad]: My Ansel bought a carved bone charm from that shack down the boardwalk. The paper tag said three copper pieces, so that is what he laid on the counter.
cora_beaudry [neutral]: The real price never fits on the little tag. If folk saw the whole bill written plain on the town board, they might walk past his door.
* What happened to him? -> cora_ansel
* We will gather the tales. -> cora_accept
* Not now. -> END

~ cora_ansel
cora_beaudry [weary]: He sits out on our back porch in his good Sunday shirt, watching the black water go by. He has not spoken a word to me in a year.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Tethered his tongue right at the root. That is nasty stitching for three coppers.
-> cora_start

~ cora_accept
cora_beaudry [neutral]: Bring me three honest accounts from people who paid the Sinner's second price. I have paper, good dark ink, and a hammer waiting.
set print_asked
quest the_sinners_small_print asked
-> END

~ cora_progress
cora_beaudry [neutral]: Have you written down what those curios truly cost, or are the folk here still buying blind?
* [if flag.small_print_read] Give her the three tales. -> cora_post
* [if flag.small_print_read] Keep the tales to ourselves. -> cora_keep
* [if not flag.small_print_read] Ask who to ask. -> cora_who
* [if flag.deal_taken_blind] [ends:the_sinners_small_print] Tell her we took a bargain before reading the tales. -> cora_lost
* Leave. -> END

~ cora_who
cora_beaudry [neutral]: Try Luckless Lou by the tables, Odell Tarrant at the boathouse, and Mama Pelletier over her stewpot. All three know someone who took a bargain HOME.
-> cora_progress

~ cora_post
approve silas_vane +3 tobin_hayward +2 rook_coldwake +2: You posted the Sinner's hidden prices to warn the town
cora_beaudry [neutral]: Thank you. Here is what I set aside for Ansel's winter coat; he has no need of wool in the heat anyway.
Narrator: She nails the three sheets deep into the cypress board, and before the iron stops ringing, a quiet queue of townsfolk has gathered to read them.
set print_outcome = "posted"
gold +60
quest the_sinners_small_print done
-> END

~ cora_keep
approve cordelia_skein +2 silas_vane +1 tobin_hayward -2: You kept the Sinner's small print to yourselves as a weapon
cora_beaudry [weary]: I see. You mean to hold the knowledge close until you face him yourselves.
cora_beaudry [sad]: Well, I cannot fault you for it. Around here, even the small print can be a weapon if you know where to point it.
set print_outcome = "kept"
quest the_sinners_small_print done
-> END

~ cora_lost
Narrator: Cora looks at you for a long, quiet moment, picks up her woven reed basket, and is gone on the next flatboat out of the bend.
set print_outcome = "lost"
quest the_sinners_small_print lost
-> END

~ lou_tale
luckless_lou [smile]: I drank a measure of Jinxed Rum for a silver wager once. Tasted like burnt molasses and riverbed mud, but it went down smooth enough.
luckless_lou [weary]: For a solid hour, every throw of the bones came up short by up to four pips, as if an unseen thumb pressed them down. I have never lost so well.
set print_lou
set print_tales += 1
if flag.print_tales >= 3
set small_print_read
quest the_sinners_small_print read
endif
-> END

~ odell_tale
odell_tarrant [afraid]: My cousin took a Jinxed Poker Chip from the Sinner's tray. He flips it across his knuckles whenever a hand turns sour, and it spares him the worst.
odell_tarrant [weary]: Only the clay chip takes its tithe out of the next good turn instead, shaving his fortune down until his pockets and his lungs feel like lead.
set print_odell
set print_tales += 1
if flag.print_tales >= 3
set small_print_read
quest the_sinners_small_print read
endif
-> END

~ mama_tale
mama_pelletier [weary]: My sister's girl bought a green bottle of Haint Hooch to ease her toothache. Took one swallow in the kitchen and stepped clean through the pantry wall.
mama_pelletier [sad]: Left her apron caught on a nail, and walked right out into some other parish. We have not seen hide nor shadow of her since.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Trans-planar displacement from a single swallow of spirits. I must have a drop for my vials.
set print_mama
set print_tales += 1
if flag.print_tales >= 3
set small_print_read
quest the_sinners_small_print read
endif
-> END

~ board
Narrator: The damp cypress tally board smells of rust and river fog, pinned over with faded slips naming who bought what curio and what grief came of it.
* [if flag.small_print_read and not flag.print_outcome] Post the three tales here. -> post_board
* Leave. -> END

~ post_board
Narrator: You drive the nails home through all three pages, and within the minute a silent crowd of bayou folk has gathered with their lanterns to read.
set print_outcome = "posted"
quest the_sinners_small_print done
-> END
